(----------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 150:  Top of a cell.  This is bounded above by
a power wire, and below by ground.  Origin is the center
of the power contact of the leftmost, or pattern, inverter.
The center of the power wire is [*,0].  The center of the ground
wire is [*,-23].

Top of the cell is top of power wire: 2, except that the
clock herniates in two places, going up to 5.  The herniae
are [-15,5] to [7,5] and [39,5] to [53,5].
Contacts to diffusion can be placed on the power wire with centers
from [16,0] to [32,0].

Bottom of the cell is the bottom of the ground wire: -25.
Contacts to diffusion can be placed along the ground wire with
centers from [13,-25] to [21,-25].

The left edge is -15.  P and S both overshoot the left edge by lambda.
clock enters from left at [-15,3] to [-15,5]
	or from above at [-15,5] to [7,5]
power enters from left at [-2,-15] to [2,-15].
P enters from left at -6 to -8.
S leaves from left at -14 to -18.
ground enters from left at -21 to -25.

The right edge is at 75.  power, ground, p, and s are at the same
levels here as on the left edge.  The clock leaves from the bottom
at [68,-25] to [70,-25].

The code is divided into 5 sections:
	power and ground
	p
	d
	s
	clock
Within each section, components are specified from left to right.);
DS 150 300 1;  (units of lambda);
LNM;  B 90,4 30,0;	(power wire);
      B 90,4 30,-23;	(ground wire);

(** p--pattern from left to right on top **);
(see clock section for pass gate at input);
C 1 R 0,-1 T -8,-8;	(contact from pdiff to ppoly);
LNP;  B 4,2 T -8,-12;	(connection to inverter input);
       B 6,2 -7,-14;
C 101 T 0,0;		(p inverter);
   LND;  B 2,4 0,-19;	(connection to ground);
	C 2 T 0,-23;	(ground contact);
LNM;  B 12,4 12,-8;	(output from the p inverter);
C 2 T 20,-8;		(contact to = gate for controlled p);
LNM;  B 12,4 28,-8;	(connection between contacts);
C 11 T 31,-9;		(contact for p control of = gate);
(* controlled p--part of = gate.  This is p gated by s *);
	(gate is described in s section);
	LND;  B 4,2 24,-17;	(path in diffusion from gate to joint);
	      B 2,6 27,-19;
	      B 14,2 33,-23;
	LNP;  B 2,12 30,-15;	(connection from contact to gate);
LNM;  B 6,4 36,-8;	(connection from contact to bridge of s);
      B 2,12 40,-12;
      B 2,12 41,-12;

(** d--result goes top to bottom **);
(see clock section for pass gate at input);
LND;  B 2,18 10,-7;	(d runs vertically straight through);
      B 4,2 8,-16;	(jogs to the left);
      B 2,2 10,-16;
      B 2,10 7,-20;	(and continues);

(** s--string from right to left **);
LNM;  B 8,4 -12,-16;	(s output from cell in metal);
      B 4,4 -7,-16;	(connect bridge of p gate to s output);
LNM;  B 4,4 11,-16;	(connect bridge of p gate to s at contact);
C 11 T 14,-16;		(contact from s to poly for = control);
LNP;  B 2,2 15,-13;	(connection from contact to transistor);
C 12 T 21,-13;		(2/8 for s control of p on = gate);
LNM;  B 16,4 24,-16;	(connection between contacts);
C 2 T 34,-16;		(contact for controlled s to = gate);
C 12 T 36,-20;		(2/8 for p control of s on = gate);
LND;  B 2,4 35,-12;	(connection from s inverter output to contact);
      B 12,2 42,-11;
C 101 T 46,0;		(s inverter);
   LND;  B 12,4 T 50,-19;	(connection to ground contact);
	C 2 T 54,-23;	(ground contact);

(** clock **);
C 5 R 0,1 T -13,-7;	(clock gate on p input);
LNP;  B 2,8 -13,0;	(clock input);
      B 22,2 -4,4;	(clock goes around p inverter);
      B 2,8 6,0;	(and down to the d input);
C 5 T 10,-3;		(clock gate on d input);
LNP;  B 2,2 13,-3;	(clock leaves d gate);
      B 28,2 26,-4;	(over to s inverter);
      B 2,8 40,-1;	(up);
DF;

(ckp lost big trying to understand the complete definition of
symbol 150.  I am therefore forced to split it into two symbols.
This is the second half of the top half of a cell.  The split
is nowhere convenient, but I'll once again divide this into 5
parts.);
DS 151 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 150 T 0,0;		(get first part.  origin in same spot);

(** p **);
LNM;  B 2,12 56,-12;	(p goes back up from bridge);
      B 2,12 57,-12;
LNM;  B 8,2 59,-7;	(connect to contact);
      B 8,2 59,-6;
C 2 T 64, -7;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;  B 6,2 69,-7;	(output in diffusion);
      B 4,2 73,-7;

(** s **);
LNP;  B 2,2 51,-14;	(connect to s inverter input);
      B 2,2 51,-15;
      B 10,2 56,-15;
C 1 M X T 64,-16;	(contact from diffusion to poly);
C 2 T 73,-16;		(contact from metal to diffusion);

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 14,2 46,4;	(clock goes around s inverter);
      B 2,8 52,0;	(and down);
      B 4,2 55,-3;	(jog over to miss side contact);
      B 2,8 56,-8;
      B 12,2 63,-11;	(over to s control);
      B 2,2 69,-11;
C 5 R 0,1 T 69,-15;	(pass gate for s input);
LNP;  B 2,8 69,-21;	(down and out);

DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------------);
(This is a description of the pattern matcher comparator cell);

(This cell has two versions:  one for normal input, and one for
inverted input.  There is one clock line controlling the cell, and
opposite versions are expected to be controlled by opposite phases
of the two phase clock.  This description of input and output
connections applies to both versions of the cell.

Here is a schematic view of the paths through the cell:

ccccc            ccccc
5555c55d555555555c555c5555
    c  d         c   c
    cccdcccccccccc   cc
       d              c
pppppppdppppppppppppppcpp
       d              c
       d              c
sssssssdsssssssssssssscss
       d              c
     | d              c
0000-+-d00000000000000c00
     | d              c
       d              c
bbbbbbbdbbbbbbbbbbbbbbcbb
       d              c
       d              ccc
5555555d55555555555555555

The meanings of the symbols are:
	c:	clock
	5:	power
	0:	ground
	b:	bridge--this is just a path across the cell
	+:	origen of the coordinate system used to describe cell
	p:	pattern
	s:	string
	d:	downward result.

In this description, lambda is 3 microns.  The cell is 88 lambda wide,
and 49 lambda high.  The origen is the center of the ground contact for
the p inverter.  With respect to this origen, the left edge is at -16,
the right edge is at 72, the center of the lower power wire is -26,
the center of the upper power wire is 23, and the clock extends above
the upper power wire to 28.

Now we describe the connections.
Clock:	connected on left edge in poly from <-16,26> to <-16,28>
	connected on right edge in poly from <72,-23> to <72,-21>

Power1:	connected on left in metal from <-16,21> to <-16,25>
	on right in metal from <72,21> to <72,25>

p:	left in diffusion from <-16,15> to <-16,17>
	right in diffusion from <72,15> to <72,17>

s:	left in metal from <-16,5> to <-16,9>
	right in metal,diffusion, and contact from <72,5> to <72,9>

Ground:	left in metal from <-16,-2> to <-16,2>
	right in metal from <72,-2> to <72, 2>

Bridge:	left in metal from <-16,-16> to <-16,-12>
	right in metal from <72,-16> to <72,-12>

Power2:	left in metal from <-16,-24> to <-16,-28>
	right in metal from <72,-24> to <72,-28>

d:	above in diffusion from <9,25> to <11,25>
	below in diffusion from <9,-28> to <11,-28>


A pad may be placed connecting the bridge to the clock at <69,-14>);

(Symbol 160:  Negative cell.  This is the complicated one.
Origin is at the center of the ground pad of the p, or leftmost
inverter.);
(This is the negative pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with positive pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 2 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs pbar from the
left, sbar from the right, and dbar from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	p out := NOT pbar in
	s out := NOT sbar in
	d out := NOT  [dbar in  OR NOT  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);


DS 160 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(the top half);

(** NOR gate **);
LND;  B 2,4 7,-4;	(dbar enters from the top);
      B 6,2 5,-6;	(connection to contact);
C 1 M X T 0,-7;		(contact diffusion to poly);
LND;  B 2,2 -8,-3;	(connection to pulldown);

C 2 T -8,0;		(ground contact for d half of nor);
C 3 T -8,-6;		(2/6 pulldown for d half);
LND;  B 2,6 -8,-11;	(connect to pullup);
      B 20,2 2,-13;

C 2 T 14,0;		(ground contact for not= half of nor);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-4;	(connect ground contact to pulldown);
C 14 T 14,-9;		(2/3 pulldown on not= half);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-14;	(connect pulldown to pullup);
C 13 M Y T 15,-20;	(6/2 pullup with side contact);
LND;  B 2,2 15,-25;	(connect pullup to contact);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nor gate);

LND;  B 4,2 11,-15;	(connect d out to inverter);
LND;  B 2,8 10,-20;	(d goes out the bottom);

(** = inverter **);
C 2 T 21,0;		(ground contact for = inverter);
LND;  B 2,2 22,-3;	(connect contact to pulldown);
      B 10,2 26,-5;
      B 2,2 30,-12;
C 5 T 30,-8;			(2/2 pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 30,-19;	(8/2 pullup for = inverter);
C 2 T 30,-26;		(power contact for inverter);

LNP;  B 2,8 26,-16;	(inverter output);
      B 4,2 25,-12;	(connect to nor gate input);
      B 2,4 23,-11;
      B 6,2 21,-9;

(** The rest of the = gate **);
LND;  B 4,4 38,-3;	(connect top part to pullup);
      B 12,4 42,-4;
C 16 M Y T 46,-12;	(8/2 pullup on = gate);
LND;  B 18,2 54,-18;	(connect pullup to power);
      B 2,6 62,-21;
C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact);

LNP;  B 4,2 35,-8;	(= gate output to inverter input);
      B 8,2 39,-9;

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 2,20 69,-12;	(clock goes straight down);
      B 8,2 72,-22;	(and over to connect to next cell);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 24,4 -4,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 4,8 10,-12;	(up to miss NOR gate contact);
      B 36,4 26,-7;	(over NOR gate and inverter);
LNM;  B 4,12 42,-14;	(down to miss =gate);
      B 20,4 50,-18;	(over to the right);
	B 20,4 66,-14;	(and out);
DF;

(Symbol 161:  Negative cell, with extended = gate pullup.
Origin is at the center of the ground pad of the p, or leftmost
inverter.);
(This is the negative pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with positive pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 2 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs pbar from the
left, sbar from the right, and dbar from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	p out := NOT pbar in
	s out := NOT sbar in
	d out := NOT  [dbar in  OR NOT  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);


DS 161 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(the top half);

(** NOR gate **);
LND;  B 2,4 7,-4;	(dbar enters from the top);
      B 6,2 5,-6;	(connection to contact);
C 1 M X T 0,-7;		(contact diffusion to poly);
LND;  B 2,2 -8,-3;	(connection to pulldown);

C 2 T -8,0;		(ground contact for d half of nor);
C 3 T -8,-6;		(2/6 pulldown for d half);
LND;  B 2,6 -8,-11;	(connect to pullup);
      B 20,2 2,-13;

C 2 T 14,0;		(ground contact for not= half of nor);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-4;	(connect ground contact to pulldown);
C 14 T 14,-9;		(2/3 pulldown on not= half);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-14;	(connect pulldown to pullup);
C 13 M Y T 15,-20;	(6/2 pullup with side contact);
LND;  B 2,2 15,-25;	(connect pullup to contact);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nor gate);

LND;  B 4,2 11,-15;	(connect d out to inverter);
LND;  B 2,8 10,-20;	(d goes out the bottom);

(** = inverter **);
C 2 T 21,0;		(ground contact for = inverter);
LND;  B 2,2 22,-3;	(connect contact to pulldown);
      B 10,2 26,-5;
      B 2,2 30,-12;
C 5 T 30,-8;			(2/2 pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 30,-19;	(8/2 pullup for = inverter);
C 2 T 30,-26;		(power contact for inverter);

LNP;  B 2,8 26,-16;	(inverter output);
      B 4,2 25,-12;	(connect to nor gate input);
      B 2,4 23,-11;
      B 6,2 21,-9;

(** The rest of the = gate **);
LND;  B 4,4 38,-3;	(connect top part to pullup);
      B 12,4 42,-4;
C 13 M Y T 46,-11;	(6/2 pullup on = gate);
LND;  B 18,2 54,-16;	(connect pullup to power);
      B 2,8 62,-20;
LNI;	B 14,6 53,-16;	(implant for extended pullup);
LNP;	B 10,6 53,-16;	(gate for extended pullup);
LNI;	B 6,6 46,-16;	(clean up corner);
LNP;	B 6,6 46,-16;

C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact);

LNP;  B 4,2 35,-8;	(= gate output to inverter input);
      B 8,2 39,-9;

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 2,20 69,-12;	(clock goes straight down);
      B 8,2 72,-22;	(and over to connect to next cell);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 24,4 -4,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 4,8 10,-12;	(up to miss NOR gate contact);
      B 36,4 26,-7;	(over NOR gate and inverter);
LNM;  B 4,12 42,-14;	(down to miss =gate);
      B 20,4 50,-18;	(over to the right);
	B 20,4 66,-14;	(and out);
DF;


(------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 170:  positive comparitor cell.  Origin is center of ground
pad of leftmost inverter.);
(This is the positive pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with negative pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 1 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs p from the
left, s from the right, and d from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	pbar out := NOT p in
	sbar out := NOT s in
	dbar out := NOT  [d in  AND  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);

DS 170 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(top half of cell);

(** nand gate **);
C 2 T 16,0;		(ground contact for nand gate);
LND;  B 4,2 16,-3;	(connection from ground to pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-6;		(first pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-10;		(second pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 18,-19;	(8/2 pullup);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nand gate);

(** d from top half **);
LND;  B 2,6 7,-4;	(connection from input to contact);
C 1 R 0,-1 T 6,-8;	(butting contact to gate input);
LNP;  B 4,2 10,-10;	(connection to gate input);

LND;  B 8,2 13,-13;	(nand gate output);
      B 2,10 10,-19;	(connect d to next cell down);

(** continuation of = gate from top half **);
LND;  B 6,4 34,-3;	(connection from top half);
LNP;  B 6,2 25,-6;	(connection to input of nand gate);
      B 2,6 29,-8;
C 16 M Y T 32,-12;	(8/2 pullup);
LND;  B 2,6 32,-21;	(connection to power contact);
C 2 T 32,-26;		(power contact for = gate);

(** clock **);
LNP;   B 2,20 69,-12;	(drop straight down from the top half);
	B 8,2 72,-22;	(connect to lower right);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 14,4 -8,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 20,4 2,-18;	(up to miss butting contact);
LNM;  B 4,12 14,-14;	(up to cross over nand gate);
      B 16,4 20,-7;	(cross over);
      B 4,12 29,-11;	(down to cross = gate);
      B 24,4 39,-16;	(across = gate);
      B 32,4 60,-14;	(out to the right);
DF;


(Symbol 171:  positive comparitor cell.  Origin is center of ground
pad of leftmost inverter.  This has the extended = pullup.);
(This is the positive pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with negative pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 1 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs p from the
left, s from the right, and d from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	pbar out := NOT p in
	sbar out := NOT s in
	dbar out := NOT  [d in  AND  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);

DS 171 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(top half of cell);

(** nand gate **);
C 2 T 16,0;		(ground contact for nand gate);
LND;  B 4,2 16,-3;	(connection from ground to pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-6;		(first pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-10;		(second pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 18,-19;	(8/2 pullup);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nand gate);

(** d from top half **);
LND;  B 2,6 7,-4;	(connection from input to contact);
C 1 R 0,-1 T 6,-8;	(butting contact to gate input);
LNP;  B 4,2 10,-10;	(connection to gate input);

LND;  B 8,2 13,-13;	(nand gate output);
      B 2,10 10,-19;	(connect d to next cell down);

(** continuation of = gate from top half **);
LND;  B 6,4 34,-3;	(connection from top half);
LNP;  B 6,2 25,-6;	(connection to input of nand gate);
      B 2,6 29,-8;
C 13 M Y T 32,-11;	(6/2 pullup);
LND;	B 28,2 47,-16;	(connection to power contact);
	B 2,10 62,-20;
LNI;	B 14,6 40,-16;	(Implant for extended = gate);
LNP;	B 10,6 40,-16;	(Gate for pullup);
LNI;	B 6,6 32,-16;	(clean up corner);
LNP;	B 6,6 32,-16;
LND;	B 2,2 32,-16;
C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact for = gate);

(** clock **);
LNP;   B 2,20 69,-12;	(drop straight down from the top half);
	B 8,2 72,-22;	(connect to lower right);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 14,4 -8,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 20,4 2,-18;	(up to miss butting contact);
LNM;  B 4,12 14,-14;	(up to cross over nand gate);
      B 16,4 20,-7;	(cross over);
      B 4,12 29,-11;	(down to cross = gate);
      B 24,4 39,-16;	(across = gate);
      B 32,4 60,-14;	(out to the right);
DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------);

(Pad hookup for one cell.  There are 9 pads for a
cell.  Starting at the upper left, and going clockwise, they are:
	ground input:
	P input
	D input
	S input
	<Symbol goes here>
	p output	<at the side>
	power input
	D output
	clock input
	S output

);
DS 210 300 1;	(units of lambda);

(** Power hookup **);
(power pad to P out pad);
LNM;	B 92,8 378,-104;	(right from power pad);
	B 8,12 420,-94;		(up to output pad);

(cell hookup);
LNM;	B 36,8 242,-104;	(horizontal out of power pad);
	B 8,88 228,-56;		(up to go around D out pad);
	B 144,8 160,-8;		(over to bus bar);
LNM;	B 88,4 28,-26;		(lowest power wire);
	B 16,4 80,23;		(hook top to bus bar);
	B 16,4 80,-26;		(hook bottom to busbar);
	B 8,50 84,-2;		(vertical bus bar);

(** Ground hookup **);
LNM;	B 24,8 -24,44;	(Ground pad to P in pad);
LNM;	B 24,8 104,44;	(P in pad to Din pad);
LNM;	B 24,8 232,44;	(D in pad to S in pad);
LNM;	B 8,12 252,34;	(S in pad to P out pad);
LNM;	B 8,64 -100,8;	(Ground pad to S out pad);
LNM;	B 4,26 -30,-11;	(S out pad to cell ground);
	B 16,4 -20,0;
LNM;	B 8,56 -32,-52;	(S out pad to clock in pad);
	B 20,8 -20,-76;
LNM;	B 16,8 100,-76;		(Clock in pad to D out pad);
	B 8,56 112,-52;

(** P input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 -14,38;	(out of pad to contact);
C 2 T -14,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 4,4 -18,34;	(to the left);
	B 4,20 -22,26;	(down to input);
C 2 T -22,16;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 4,2 -18,16;	(into cell);
(** P output hookup **);
LND;	B 28,4 86,16;	(diffusion out of cell);
C 2 T 102,16;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 142,4 173,16;	(metal over to the right);
LNM;	B 4,40 242,-4;	(down to pad);
C 11 T 242,-24;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 246,-24;	(to output pad);

(**S input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 242,38;	(diffusion path to contact);
C 2 T 242,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 100,4 190,34;	(metal run to the left);
	B 20,4 130,34;
	B 4,4 122,30;	(down);
	B 32,4 108,26;	(to the left again);
	B 4,16 94,18;	(down to contact);
C 2 T 94,8;		(contact from metal to gate input);
LND;	B 20,2 82,8;	(gate input in diffusion);
(** S output hookup **);
LNM;	B 74,4 -53,7;	(From cell leftward to pad);
	B 4,22 -88,-6;	(Down to contact);
C 11 T -88,-18;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 -88,-22;	(poly into pad);

(** D input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 114,38;	(diffusion path to contact);
C 2 T 114,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 102,4 61,34;	(metal run to input);
C 2 T 10,34;		(contact back to diffusion);
LND;	B 2,12 10,28;	(into cell);
(** D output hookup **);
LND;	B 2,8 10,-28;	(Leave cell in diffusion);
C 2 T 10,-34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 84,4 54,-34;	(metal run to end of cell);
	B 4,12 94 -26;	(up to go around output pad);
	B 76,4 130,-18;	(over to pad);
C 11 T 168,-18;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 168,-22;	(down to gate);

(** clock hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 -14,-70;	(diffusion path from pad to contact);
C 2 T -14,-66;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 8,4 -20,-66;	(path up to metal bridge);
	B 4,52 -22,-38;
	B 8,4 -16,-14;
C 11 T 69 -14;		(contact from metal to poly);

(*Upper row of pads:  gnd, din, pout, sin *);
C 10006 T -152,168;	(Ground);
C 10004 M X T 104,168;	(P in);
C 10004 M X T 232,168;	(D in);
C 10004 M X T 360,168;	(S in);

(* lower row of pads *);
C 10002 M Y T -152,-200;	(S out);
C 10004 M X M Y T 104,-200;	(clock in);
C 10002 M Y T 104,-200;		(D out);
C 10005 M Y T 232,-200;		(Vdd in);

(* Rightmost pad *);
C 10002 R 0,-1 T 424,40;	(P out);
DF;

(A negative cell, hooked up);
DS 220 300 1;		(units don't matter, but lambda nonetheless);
C 160 T 0,0;		(The cell);
C 210 T 0,0;		(The hookup);
LNM;	B 56,12 380,100;	(Symbol);
DF;

(A positive cell, hooked up);
DS 230 300 1;
C 170 T 0,0;		(The cell);
C 210 T 0,0;		(The hookup);
LNM;	B 56,12 380,100;	(Symbol);
	B 12,56 380,100;
DF;


(**Extended pullups**);
(A negative cell with extended = pullup, hooked up);
DS 240 300 1;		(units don't matter, but lambda nonetheless);
C 161 T 0,0;		(The cell);
C 210 T 0,0;		(The hookup);
LNM;	B 56,12 380,100;	(Symbol);
LNM;	B 20,20 380,-140;	(Dot to show extension);
DF;


(A positive cell with extended = pullup, hooked up);
DS 250 300 1;
C 171 T 0,0;		(The cell);
C 210 T 0,0;		(The hookup);
LNM;	B 56,12 380,100;	(Symbol);
	B 12,56 380,100;
LNM;	B 20,20 380,-140;	(Dot to show extension);
DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------);

(This is the design for the accumulator cells of the pattern
matcher.  There are two of them, one for positive input
and the other for negative input.  These cells implement
don't care characters);

(--------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 300:  The common part of the accumulator cell.
The cell is 88 lambda long, going from -24 to 64, and is 104 lambda
high, going from -20 to 84.  Here is a map of the cell:

cc   d
5c555d5555555555555555555555
 c   d
 ccccd
 c   d
xcxxxdxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
 c   d
gcgggdgggggggggggggggggggggg
 c   d   x
cc    t:= x or d  wwwwwwwwww
 c               ww  tt
5c555555555555555w5555t55555
 c               w    t
lclllllllllllllllwlllltlllll
 c     l         w    t  l
gcggggglgggggggggwggggtgglgg
 c     l         w    t  l
 c     l         w    t  l
   Store and compute result
 c                    t  l
5c55555555555555555555t55l55
 c                    t  l
rcrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrtrrlrr

gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg

Here are the meanings of the symbols:
	5:	power
	g:	ground
	d:	the character result from comparators
	x:	don't care about a match at this character
	t:	the match result computed here
	c:	right, or computation, clock phase
	w:	wrong, or regeneration, clock phase
	l:	lambda, or end of pattern
	r:	result that moves with the string.


Here are the connection levels:
ground:	Connected on both sides in 4 lambda wires centered at
		-18, 24, and 66.

power:	Connected on both sides in 4 lambda wires centered at
		0, 42, and 82.

c:		computation clock phase connected on left in 2 lambda
		high poly at 86, and in a metal-poly contact at -22,50.

w:		regeneration clock phase connected on right in metal
		4 lambda high centered at 50.

d:		comes from above in 2 lambda diffusion at 2.

x:		connected left and right in 2 lambda diffusion at 74.

l:		connected left and right in 2 lambda diffusion at 32.

r:		connected left and right in 2 lambda diffusion at -10.


);

DS 300 300 1;	(units of lambda);
(origin is at the power contact of the leftmost gate
of the flip-flop.  This code is organized into rows, from
bottom to top.  Within each row, the code goes generally
from left to right.);

(** power and ground wires **);
LNM;	B 88,4 20,-18;	(lowest ground);
	B 88,4 20,0;	(lowest power);
	B 88,4 20,24;	(middle ground);
	B 88,4 20,42;	(middle power);
	B 88,4 20,66;	(highest ground);
	B 88,4 20,82;	(highest power);

(**************************);
(** First row--R         **);
LND;	B 2,2 -24,-10;	(R leaves from the left);

C 2 T -17,0;		(power contact for R inverter);
C 13 M X T -17,-6;	(6/2 pullup);
C 3 T -18,-14;		(2/6 pulldown);
C 2 T -17,-18;		(Ground contact);

LND;	B 2,2 64,-10;		(R enters from the right);
LNP;	B 2,6 60,-5;	(NOT lambda comes from above);
C 5 R 0,1 T 60,-10;	(NOT lambda pass gate);
LND;	B 26,2 44,-10;	(Path from gate to contact);

LND;	B 2,8 40,-6;	(T hooks up to r);

C 5 R 0,1 T 28,-10;	(clock pass gate);
C 1 M X T 22,-10;	(Butting contact to gate input);
LNP;	B 2,2 20,-13;	(Down from butting contact);
	B 34,2 4,-14;	(across to inverter input);

(*clock*);
LNP;	B 2,6 -11,-5;		(down from above);
	B 26,2 1,-9;		(around the diffusion hernia);
	B 2,6 15,-7;		(up);
	B 12,2 22,-5;		(over to pass gate);
	B 2,4 28,-6;		(and down);

(*********************************);
(** Flip flop.  This is different in negative and positive cells. **);

(*left gate*);
LND;	B 2,4 -8,0;	(left input);
C 5 T -8,4;		(2/2 clock pass gate);
LND;	B 12,2 -13,7;	(over to butting contact);
C 1 R 0,1 T -17,9;		(butting contact for gate input);
LNP;	B 2,4 -17,14;	(connect to gate input);
	B 4,2 -16,16;

LNP;	B 2,6 6,23;	(right input);
	B 2,2 6,20;

LND;	B 2,2 7,12;	(gate output);
C 5 R 0,1 T 10,12;	(2/2 pass transistor for clocked output);

(Left input);
C 1 R 0,1 T 15,14;		(Butting contact from left output);
LNP;	B 2,2 18,16;		(Connect contact to left input);

(Right input);
LNP;	B 2,6 38,23;
	B 4,2 37,20;
(Cross-couple output);
LND;	B 2,4 21,10;	(out of right gate);
	B 12,2 16,7;	(to the left);
	B 2,12 11,0;	(down);
	B 20,2 2,-6;	(around power contact);
	B 2,6 -8,-4;	(and back up to left input);

(Real output);
LND;	B 2,2 38,12;	(out of side contact);
	B 2,6 40,10;	(down to transistor);
C 5 T 40,4;		(2/2 transistor controlled by lambda);
LND;	B 2,4 40,0;	(out the bottom);

(** Lambda inverter **);
C 2 T 50,0;		(power contact);
C 13 M Y T 50,7;		(6/2 pullup);
C 14 T 50,16;		(2/3 pulldown);
LND;	B 2,4 50,20;	(connect pulldown to contact);
C 2 T 50,24;		(ground contact);


LNP;	B 2,10 44,21;	(lambda comes in the top);
	B 6,2 46,16;	(input to inverter);


(*******************************);
(** Lambda from left to right *);
(inverter);
C 3 T 30,28;	(2/6 pulldown);
C 13 T 29,36;	(6/2 pullup);
C 2 T 30,42;	(Power contact);

(lambda input);
C 5 R 0,1 T -22,32;	(clock control gate);
LND;	B 20,2 T -10,32;	(diffusion to contact);
C 1 T 2,32;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,10 6,31;	(up and down);
	B 12,2 11,37;	(over above clock contact);
	B 2,10 16,33;	(down under clock bridge);
	B 10,2 20,28;	(over to inverter input);

(output);
LNM;	B 8,4 39,32;	(Metal bridge out of inverter);
LNP;	B 2,18 38,35;	(xd combination goes through);

C 1 M X T 46,32;	(Butting contact to poly and diffusion);
LNP;	B 2,4 44,28;	(Down to flip-flop);
LND;	B 16,2 56,32;	(Out to the right in diffusion);


(* Right phase clock controls lambda *);
LNP;	B 2,10 -22,39;	(in from above);
	B 2,4 -22,27;	(down to flip-flop);
(* wrong phase clock comes from above down to flip-flop*);
LND;	B 2,10 23,39;	(down from above);
C 2 T 22,32;	(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 8,4 16,32;	(metal bridge over lambda);
C 11 T 11,32;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 10,28;	(down to flip-flop);

(**********************************************);
(** Combine D and X                          **);
(D input);
LND;	B 2,10 -11,63;	(diffusion in from top);
C 1 R 0,-1 T -12,56;	(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,2 -9,54;	(connect to gate input);
	B 2,6 -7,56;

(X input);
LNP;	B 2,6 14,65;	(from above);
	B 2,2 14,62;


(output);
LND;	B 16,2 16,55;	(out to clock gate);
C 5 R 0,1 T 27,55;	(gate for wrong phase clock);
LND;	B 4,2 32,55;	(over to contact);
C 1 T 34,58;		(butting contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,16 38,52;	(down);

(******************************************************);
(** Highest level-- x from the left, d from the top **);
(x);
C 5 R 0,1 T -22,74;	(clock gate for x);
C 2 T -17,74;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 24,4 -4,74;	(metal bridge over d);
C 11 T 8,74;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 12,73;	(right from the contact);
	B 2,6 14,71;	(down to gate input);

(x inverter);
C 2 T 20,66;		(ground contact);
C 3 T 20,70;		(2/6 pulldown);
LND;	B 16,2 25,74;	(from pulldown to pullup);
	B 2,4 32,71;
	B 18,2 40,69;
	B 2,2 48,71;

(Hand-craft pullup);
LND;	B 2,10 40,75;	(channel);
LNP;	B 6,6 40,75;	(Gate);
LNI;	B 6,10 40,75;	(implant);
C 1 M X T 46,74;	(contact from channel to gate);
C 2 T 40,82;		(contact to power);

(x goes out to the right);
LND;	B 16,2 56,74;

(d);
LND;	B 2,12 2,78;	(down from above);
	B 2,2 2,72;
LND;	B 14,2 -5,72;	(to the left);
C 5 T -11,69;		(clock for d);

(** clock **);
LNP;	B 2,2 -24,86;	(in from upper left);
	B 2,10 -22,82;
LNP;	B 8,2 -18,69;	(control for d);
	B 2,4 -22,70;	(out the bottom);
DF;


(Negative accumulator cell.  This takes negative inputs, produces
positive outputs, and uses NAND gates);

DS 310 300 1;
C 300 T 0,0;		(The common stuff);

(** Phase 2 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,22 -22,15;	(enters from the top);
	B 12,2 -17,4;	(over to flip-flop gate);
	B 2,6 -11,1;	(and out the bottom);

(** Phase 1 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,12 10,20;	(enters from the top);

(** Flip-flop **);
(*left nand gate*);
C 103 T 0,0;		(The gate itself);

(*right nand gate*);
C 103 T 32,0;		(The gate);
(* cross-couple output*);
LND;	B 12,2 26,13;	(NAND gate connection);

(*Lambda comes in to inverter*);
LNP;	B 2,14 44,10;	(controls flip-flop output);

LNP;	B 4,2 58,8;	(inverter output);
	B 2,12 60,3;	(out the bottom);

(**** d NAND x ****);
C 103 T 8,42;		(The NAND gate);

(** phase 1 clock contact **);
C 11 T -22,50;
LNP;	B 2,4 -22,46;	(below);
	B 2,16 -22,60;	(and above);

(** phase 2 clock **);
LNM;	B 40,4 44,50;	(in from the right);
C 1 T 25,49;		(contact to diffusion and poly);
LNP;	B 2,2 27,52;	(up to control gate);
LND;	B 2,4 23,46;	(down to lower level);
DF;

(The positive accumulator cell.  This takes positive inputs, gives
negative outputs, and uses NOR gates.);

DS 320 300 1;
C 300 T 0,0;		(The common stuff);

(** Phase 1 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,22 -22,15;	(enters from the top);
	B 12,2 -17,4;	(over to flip-flop gate);
	B 2,6 -11,1;	(and out the bottom);

(** Phase 2 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,12 10,20;	(enters from the top);

(** Flip-flop **);
(*left nor gate*);
C 102 T 0,0;		(The gate itself);

(*right nor gate*);
C 102 T 32,0;		(The gate);

(* Lambda comes in to inverter *);
LNP;	B 8,2 57,16;	(out the other side of the inverter);
	B 2,18 60,7;	(down and out the bottom);

LNP;	B 4,2 45,6;	(inverter output);
	B 4,2 44,4;	(controls flip-flop output);


(**** d NOR x ****);

C 102 T 8,42;		(The NOR gate);

(** phase 1 clock contact **);
C 11 T -22,50;
LNP;	B 2,4 -22,46;	(below);
	B 2,16 -22,60;	(and above);

(** phase 2 clock **);
LNM;	B 40,4 44,50;	(in from the right);
C 1 T 25,49;		(contact to diffusion and poly);
LNP;	B 2,2 27,52;	(up to control gate);
LND;	B 2,4 23,46;	(down to lower level);
DF;

(------------------------------------------------------------------);

(These are the FAST accumulators.  They use the unclocked lambda
to steer signals to the r inverter.  They interface the same);
DS 301 300 1;	(units of lambda);
(origin is at the power contact of the leftmost gate
of the flip-flop.  This code is organized into rows, from
bottom to top.  Within each row, the code goes generally
from left to right.);

(** power and ground wires **);
LNM;	B 88,4 20,-18;	(lowest ground);
	B 88,4 20,0;	(lowest power);
	B 88,4 20,24;	(middle ground);
	B 12,4 -18,42;	(middle power);
	B 72,4 20,46;	(jog up and across cell);
	B 4,8 55,44;	(jog down);
	B 8,4 60,42;	(out to the right);

	B 48,4 0,66;	(highest ground);
	B 44,4 42,67;	(jogs up);
	B 4,4 62,66;	(and back down);

	B 88,4 20,82;	(highest power);

(**************************);
(** First row--R         **);
LND;	B 2,2 -24,-10;	(R leaves from the left);

C 2 T -17,0;		(power contact for R inverter);
C 13 M X T -17,-6;	(6/2 pullup);
C 3 T -18,-14;		(2/6 pulldown);
C 2 T -17,-18;		(Ground contact);

LND;	B 2,2 64,-10;		(R enters from the right);
LNP;	B 2,6 60,-5;	(NOT lambda comes from above);
C 5 R 0,1 T 60,-10;	(NOT lambda pass gate);
LND;	B 26,2 44,-10;	(Path from gate to contact);

LND;	B 2,8 40,-6;	(T hooks up to r);

C 5 R 0,1 T 28,-10;	(clock pass gate);
C 1 M X T 22,-10;	(Butting contact to gate input);
LNP;	B 2,2 20,-13;	(Down from butting contact);
	B 34,2 4,-14;	(across to inverter input);

(*clock*);
LNP;	B 2,6 -11,-5;		(down from above);
	B 26,2 1,-9;		(around the diffusion hernia);
	B 2,6 15,-7;		(up);
	B 12,2 22,-5;		(over to pass gate);
	B 2,4 28,-6;		(and down);

(*********************************);
(** Flip flop.  This is different in negative and positive cells. **);

(*left gate*);
LND;	B 2,4 -8,0;	(left input);
C 5 T -8,4;		(2/2 clock pass gate);
LND;	B 12,2 -13,7;	(over to butting contact);
C 1 R 0,1 T -17,9;		(butting contact for gate input);
LNP;	B 2,4 -17,14;	(connect to gate input);
	B 4,2 -16,16;

LNP;	B 2,6 6,23;	(right input);
	B 2,2 6,20;

LND;	B 2,2 7,12;	(gate output);
C 5 R 0,1 T 10,12;	(2/2 pass transistor for clocked output);

(Left input);
C 1 R 0,1 T 15,14;		(Butting contact from left output);
LNP;	B 2,2 18,16;		(Connect contact to left input);

(Right input);
LNP;	B 2,6 38,23;
	B 4,2 37,20;
(Cross-couple output);
LND;	B 2,4 21,10;	(out of right gate);
	B 12,2 16,7;	(to the left);
	B 2,12 11,0;	(down);
	B 20,2 2,-6;	(around power contact);
	B 2,6 -8,-4;	(and back up to left input);

(Real output);
LND;	B 2,2 38,12;	(out of side contact);
	B 2,6 40,10;	(down to transistor);
C 5 T 40,4;		(2/2 transistor controlled by lambda);
LND;	B 2,4 40,0;	(out the bottom);

(** Lambda inverter **);
C 2 T 50,0;		(power contact);
C 13 M Y T 50,7;		(6/2 pullup);
C 14 T 50,16;		(2/3 pulldown);
LND;	B 2,4 50,20;	(connect pulldown to contact);
C 2 T 50,24;		(ground contact);


LNP;	B 2,6 60,19;	(lambda comes in the top);
	B 8,2 57,16;	(inverter input);

LNP;	B 2,12 60,2;	(NOT LAMBDA goes out the bottom);

(*******************************);
(** Lambda from left to right *);
(inverter);
C 3 T 30,28;	(2/6 pulldown);
LND;	B 2,2 29,32;	(connect pullup to pulldown);

LND;	B 2,10 29,38;	(Handcraft a 6/2 pullup);
LNP;	B 6,6 29,38;
LNI;	B 6,10 29,38;
LNP;	B 8,2 36,36;	(connect gate to butting contact);
	B 2,2 39,35;
LND;	B 4,2 32,32;	(connect channel to butting contact);
C 1 T 37,32;		(butting contact);
LND;	B 2,2 29,43;	(connect pullup to power contact);
C 2 T 30,46;	(Power contact);

(lambda input);
(C 5 R 0,1 T -22,32);	(clock control gate);
(LND;	B 20,2 T -10,32);	(diffusion to contact);
C 2 T -22,32;		(contact diffusion to metal at input);
LNM;	B 4,4 -22,35;	(unclocked lambda goes up);
	B 12,4 -14,35;	(and to the right);
	B 4,8 -7,37;
	B 54,4 20,39;
C 11 T 48,39;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,10 49,32;	(down to flip flop level);
	B 12,2 55,28;
	B 2,6 60,25;

LND;	B 12,2 -14,32;	(connect to clock gate);
C 5 R 0,1 T -5,32;	(clock gate);
LND;	B 2,2 -2,32;	(connect to contact);
C 1 T 2,32;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,10 6,31;	(up and down);
	B 12,2 11,37;	(over above clock contact);
	B 2,10 16,33;	(down under clock bridge);
	B 10,2 20,28;	(over to inverter input);

(output);
(LNM;	B 8,4 39,32);	(Metal bridge out of inverter);
LNM;	B 16,4 48,32;	(metal bridge out of inverter);
C 2 T 58,32;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 4,2 62,32;	(out to the right in diffusion);
LNP;	B 2,20 43,34;	(xd combination goes through);
	B 4,2 40,25;


(* Right phase clock controls lambda *);
LNP;	B 18,2 -14,43;	(in from above);
	B 2,10 -5,39;	(down to gate);
	B 18,2 -13,28;	(down from gate to flip flop);
	B 2,4 -22,27;
(* wrong phase clock comes from above down to flip-flop*);
LND;	B 2,10 23,39;	(down from above);
C 2 T 22,32;	(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 8,4 16,32;	(metal bridge over lambda);
C 11 T 11,32;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 10,28;	(down to flip-flop);

(**********************************************);
(** Combine D and X                          **);
(D input);
LND;	B 6,2 -13,65;	(in from the top);
	B 2,4 -15,62;
C 1 R 0,-1 T -16,58;	(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 -12,57;	(into gate input);
	B 10,2 -7,58;

(X input);
LNP;	B 2,6 14,65;	(from above);
	B 6,2 12,62;

(Hook gate pullup to pulldown);
LND;	B 8,2 8,54;	(right);
	B 2,6 12,56;	(up);
	B 8,2 15,59;	(right again);

(output);
LND;	B 28,2 30,59;	(out to clock gate);
C 5 R 0,1 T 47,59;	(gate for wrong phase clock);
LNP;	B 2,2 T 47,56;	(connect gate to clock contact);
LND;	B 4,2 52,59;	(over to contact);
C 1 T 54,60;		(butting contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,16 58,52;	(down);
	B 16,2 50,44;	(and left);
	B 2,2 58,44;

(** computation phase clock contact **);
C 11 T -22,50;
LNP;	B 2,4 -22,46;	(below);
	B 2,16 -22,60;	(and above);

(** regeneration phase clock **);
LNM;	B 4,4 62,50;	(in from the right);
	B 20,2 54,53;	(jog up);
	B 20,2 54,52;
C 1 T 45,53;		(contact to diffusion and poly);
LND;	B 20,2 32,52;	(left);
LND;	B 2,8 23,48;	(down to lower level);

(******************************************************);
(** Highest level-- x from the left, d from the top **);
(x);
C 5 R 0,1 T -22,74;	(clock gate for x);
C 2 T -17,74;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 24,4 -4,74;	(metal bridge over d);
C 11 T 8,74;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 12,73;	(right from the contact);
	B 2,6 14,71;	(down to gate input);

(x inverter);
C 2 T 20,66;		(ground contact);
C 3 T 20,70;		(2/6 pulldown);
LND;	B 16,2 25,74;	(from pulldown to pullup);
	B 2,4 32,71;
	B 18,2 40,69;
	B 2,2 48,71;

(Hand-craft pullup);
LND;	B 2,10 40,75;	(channel);
LNP;	B 6,6 40,75;	(Gate);
LNI;	B 6,10 40,75;	(implant);
C 1 M X T 46,74;	(contact from channel to gate);
C 2 T 40,82;		(contact to power);

(x goes out to the right);
LND;	B 16,2 56,74;

(d);
LND;	B 2,12 2,78;	(down from above);
	B 2,2 2,72;
LND;	B 14,2 -5,72;	(to the left);
C 5 T -11,69;		(clock for d);

(** clock **);
LNP;	B 2,2 -24,86;	(in from upper left);
	B 2,10 -22,82;
LNP;	B 8,2 -18,69;	(control for d);
	B 2,4 -22,70;	(out the bottom);
DF;


(FAST);
(Negative accumulator cell.  This takes negative inputs, produces
positive outputs, and uses NAND gates);

DS 311 300 1;
C 301 T 0,0;		(The common stuff);

(** Phase 2 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,22 -22,15;	(enters from the top);
	B 12,2 -17,4;	(over to flip-flop gate);
	B 2,6 -11,1;	(and out the bottom);

(** Phase 1 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,12 10,20;	(enters from the top);

(** Flip-flop **);
(*left nand gate*);
C 103 T 0,0;		(The gate itself);

(*right nand gate*);
C 103 T 32,0;		(The gate);
(* cross-couple output*);
LND;	B 12,2 26,13;	(NAND gate connection);

(*Lambda bar comes in to inverter*);
LNP;	B 2,8 60,12;	(out the bottom to control r);
LNP;	B 4,2 44,4;	(output controls flip-flop);
	B 4,2 45,5;

(**** d NAND x ****);
C 2 T 17,46;		(hand craft it.  power contact);
C 16 M Y T 17,53;	(pullup);
C 12 T 3,58;		(one pulldown);
C 12 T 3,62;		(another pulldown);
C 2 T 4,66;		(ground contact);
DF;

(The positive accumulator cell.  This takes positive inputs, gives
negative outputs, and uses NOR gates.);

DS 321 300 1;
C 301 T 0,0;		(The common stuff);

(** Phase 1 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,22 -22,15;	(enters from the top);
	B 12,2 -17,4;	(over to flip-flop gate);
	B 2,6 -11,1;	(and out the bottom);

(** Phase 2 clock **);
LNP;	B 2,12 10,20;	(enters from the top);

(** Flip-flop **);
(*left nor gate*);
C 102 T 0,0;		(The gate itself);

(*right nor gate*);
C 102 T 32,0;		(The gate);

(* Lambda comes in to inverter *);
LNP;	B 2,14 44,10;	(controls flip-flop output);
	B 2,2 46,16;


LNP;	B 6,2 58,8;	(inverter output goes out the bottom);


(**** d NOR x ****);

C 2 T 17,46;		(hand craft it.  power contact);
LND;	B 2,2 17,48;	(connect power contact to pullup);
C 13 M Y T 17,54;	(pullup);
LND;	B 12,2 -2,54;	(connection to left pulldown);
C 3 T -5,58;		(2/6 pulldown for left branch);
LND;	B 2,4 -6,62;	(connection to ground contact);
	B 10,2 -2,65;
LND;	B 2,4 4,57;	(connection to right pulldown);
C 3 T 4,62;		(2/6 pulldown for right branch);
C 2 T 4,66;		(ground contact for right branch);
DF;

(----------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 330:  Negative accumulator cell, translated to sit below
a comparator cell that is at 0,0.  This is the bottom row of a
complete pattern matcher);
(uses FAST accumulator);

DS 330 300 1;
C 311 T 8,-108;
DF;

(Symbol 340:  Positive accumulator cell, translated the same way.);
(uses FAST accumulator);
DS 340 300 1;
C 321 T 8,-108;
DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------------);

(----------------------------------------------------------------);
(Symbol 350:  hookup for accumulator cells);
(This is a hookup to pads for a single accumulator of the pattern
matcher.  It works for both negative and positive versions.  Each
input or output of the cell is connected to a pad, and the outputs
of both inverters in the flip flop are also connected to pads.
There are 14 pads.  Starting in the upper left and going clockwise,
the pads are:

	<upper row, left to right>
	c	in	this is the "right", or computation clock, phase
	d	in	the match result from the comparators above
	x	out	don't care out to the right
	d OR x	out	the result of an internal computation <inverted>.
	w	in	the "wrong", or regeneration, clock phase
	Vdd

	<right side>
	lambda out	end of pattern, out to the right

	<bottom row, right to left>
	Ground
	t old	out	the t that affects the result
	r	in	result string from the right
	r	out	out to the left
	t new	out	the t that is computed <inverted>
	lambda	in	end of pattern, from the left

	<left side>
	x	in	don't care, from the left.

In use, the three output pads for internal state need not be connected.);

DS 350 300 1;
(** Top row of pads **);
C 10004 T -432,280;	(right clock in);
C 10004 T -304,280;	(d in);
C 10002 T -176,280;		(x out);
C 10002 T -48,280;		(d OR x);
C 10004 M X T 208,280;		(wrong clock);
C 10005 T 208,280;		(Vdd);

(** Rightmost pad **);
C 10002 R 0,-1 T 336,156;

(** Bottom row of pads **);
C 10006 M Y T 208,-200;	(ground);
C 10002 M Y T 80,-200;	(t old out);
C 10004 M Y T -48,-200;	(r in);
C 10002 M Y T -176,-200;	(r out);
C 10002 M Y T -304,-200;	(t new out);
C 10004 M Y T -432,-200;	(lambda in);


(** leftmost pad **);
C 10004 R 0,1 T -432,0;	(x in);

(** Right clock, or c, input hookup **);
LNP;	B 24,2 -32,86;	(into top left corner of cell);
	B 4,4 -46,85;	(from contact);
C 11 T -46,82;		(connection from metal to poly);
LNM;	B 240,4 -168,82;	(metal wire from pad);
	B 4,56 -286,112;
LND;	B 2,8 -314,148;	(out of pad);
	B 30,4 -300,142;
C 2 T -286,142;		(contact to metal);

(** D input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 2,86;	(into top of cell);
C 2 T 2,90;		(contact from metal to diffusion);
LNM;	B 48,4 -24,90;	(from the left in metal);
	B 136,4 -116,90;	(From the pad);
	B 4,56 -186,116;
C 2 T -186,146;		(contact from diffusion to metal);
LND;	B 2,4 -186,150;		(out of input pad);

(** X output hookup **);
LND;	B 2,18 62,82;	(out of right edge of cell);
C 2 T 62,90;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 52,4 34,90;	(to the left);
	B 4,4 10,94;	(up to miss D contact);
	B 60,4 -18,98;	(left again);
	B 64,4 -80,98;	(left still more);
C 11 T -112,98;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 -112,102;	(into output pad);

(** D or X output hookup **);
LNM;	B 16,2 64,60;	(metal wire from butting contact);
	B 16,2 64,59;
	(B 20,4 46,60);	(can hook to either 300 or 301);
	(B 2,4 38,58);
	(B 2,4 37,58);
C 2 T 70,58;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 12,4 78,58;	(tunnel under bus bar);
C 2 T 86,58;		(contact back to metal);
LNM;	B 4,40 86,78;	(up);
C 11 T 86,98;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 6,2 81,98;	(connect to input of gate);

(level restoring inverter);
C 2 T 74,82;		(power contact);
C 13 M X M Y T 74,89;	(pullup);
C 3 T 74,98;		(pulldown);
LND;	B 4,4 74,102;	(connect to contact);
C 2 T 74,106;		(ground contact);
LNM;	B 8,4 68,82;	(hookup power to it);

LNM;	B 52,4 46,98;	(gate output to pad);
	B 4,4 70,96;
C 11 T 18,98;		(contact metal to poly);
LNP;	B 2,8 16,100;	(poly into output pad);

(** Wrong clock, or w, hookup **);
C 2 T 62,50;		(contact from diffusion );
LND;	B 20,4 74,50;	(tunnel under ground);
C 2 T 86,50;		(back to metal);
LNM;	B 4,4 90,50;	(from wire to contact pad);
LNM;	B 4,100 94,98;	(metal from pad);
C 2 T 90,146;		(contact from diffusion to metal);
LND;	B 2,4 90,150;	(diffusion from pad);

(** Lambda out hookup **);
LND;	B 24,4 72,34;	(tunnel under ground);
C 2 T 86,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 16,4 96,34;	(to the right in metal);
	B 4,56 102,64;	(up);
	B 52,4 126,92;	(right to pad);
C 11 T 154,92;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 158,92;	(into pad);

(** t old out hookup **);
LNM;	B 4,6 36,15;	(Metal bridge over gate of lambda inverter);
	B 34,2 51,17;
	B 34,2 51,18;
C 2 T 66,14;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 16,4 76,14;	(tunnel under ground);
C 2 T 86,14;		(contact back to metal);
LNM;	B 56,4 116,14;	(to pad in metal);
C 11 T 144,14;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,36 144,-6;	(poly into pad);

(** R in Hookup **);
LND;	B 8,2 66,-10;(path in diffusion from pad);
	B 2,70 70,-44;

(** R out hookup **);
LND;	B 4,2 -26,-10;	(out in diffusion);
C 2 T -30,-10;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 16,4 -40,-10;	(To -48 in metal);
LNM;	B 64,4 -80,-10;	(To pad);
C 11 T -112,-10;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,12 -112,-18;	(poly into pad);

(** T new out hookup **);
LNM;	B 6,4 -21,10;	(metal bridge over clock);
C 2 T -26,10;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 16,2 -36,10;	(tunnel under power);
C 2 T -46,10;		(contact back to metal);
LNM;	B 4,12 -46,2;	(down to metal wire);
LNM;	B 104,4 -98,-2;	(over toward pad);
C 11 T -150,-2;
LNP;	B 2,16 -150,-11;	(down to inverter input);
	B 6,2 -154,-18;

(level restoring inverter);
C 2 T -160,26;		(power contact);
LND;	B 2,28 -160,10;	(connect contact to pullup);
C 13 M X T -160,-8;	(pullup);
LND;	B 2,12 -160,-18;	(finish inverter hookup);
C 3 T -160,-18;	(pulldown);
LND;	B 4,4 160,-22;
C 2 T -160,-26;	(ground contact);

LNM;	B 76,4 -202,-10;	(inverter output to pad);
C 11 T -240,-10;		(contact to poly);
LNP;	B 2,12 -240,-18;	(into pad);

(** lambda in hookup **);
LND;	B 24,2 -36,32;	(diffusion tunnel under power);
C 2 T -46,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 8,4 -52,34;	(jog left);
	B 4,28 -54,18;	(down to long wire);
	B 180,4 -146,6;	(long wire);
	B 16,4 -240,6;
	B 4,24 -250,-4;
	B 64,4 -280,-18;
C 2 T -314,-18;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 2,52 -314,-46;	(out of input pad);

(** X in hookup **);
LND;	B 20,2 -34,74;	(Diffusion tunnel under power);
C 2 T -46,74;		(Contact to metal);
LNM;	B 252,4 -174,74;	(metal wire from pad);
	B 4,40, -298,96;
C 2 T -298,118;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 4,2 -302,118;	(diffusion out of pad);

(** Power hookup **);
LNM;	B 8,116 332,214;	(power pad to  lambda out);
LNM;	B 8,228 332,-86;	(lambda out to ground pad);

(cell);
LNM;	B 8,86 -36,41;	(left power wire);
	B 8,4 -28,82;	(hook top cell wire);
	B 8,4 -28,42;	(middle);
	B 8,4 -28,0;	(bottom);
LNM;	B 24,12 -52,54;	(power wire to cell);
	B 12,24,-70,48;
	B 196,12 -162,30;
	B 12,32 -266,20;	(up from gap);
	B 164,12 -342,-2;	(right through gap);

LNM;	B 8,152 -428,204;	(c in to x in);
LNM;	B 8,200 -428,-100;	(x in to lambda in);

(** Ground hookup **);
LNM;	B 8,76 164,14;	(connect t old out to lambda out);
LNM;	B 8,8 164,148;	(Lambda out to w in);
LNM;	B 8,56 72,132;	(d or x out to wrong clock in);
	B 24,8 80,156;
LNM;	B 24,8 -48,108;	(Xout to DorX out);
LNM;	B 8,56 -168,132;	(D in to Xout);
	B 16,8 -180,156;
(hook up D in, C in, and lambda in);
LNM;	B 24,8 -304,156;
	B 8,40 -308,136;

LNM;	B 8,56 200,-52;	(Connect ground pad to told out);
	B 16,8 212,-76;
(cell);
LNM;	B 32,8	76,-28;	(from told out pad);
	B 16,4 72,-22;
	B 8,52 60,-46;	(down to r in pad);
LNM;	B 8,72 76,16;	(Right wire on cell);
	B 16,4 72,66;	(connect upper ground to bus bar);
	B 4,12 78,58;
	B 8,4 68,24;	(middle);
	B 8,4 68,-18;	(bottom);

LNM;	B 8,56 -56,-52;	(r in to r out);
	B 16,8 -44,-76;
LNM;	B 32,8 -176,-28;	(r out to t new);
LNM;	B 8,56 -296,-52;	(t new to lambda in);
	B 16,8 -308,-76;
DF;

(Symbol 360:	negative accumulator cell, hooked to pads);
(uses FAST accumulator);
DS 360 300 1;
C 311 T 0,0;		(negative cell);
C 350 T 0,0;		(hookup);
